==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAudit  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAudit.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyAudit allows the model to produce a DeletedTask with no AuditDeleted entry, directly violating the append-only invariant that audit entries outlive their task row. The injection forces exactly that scenario.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditOutlivesTask
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditOutlivesTask: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Removing F_OwnershipBasedAccess allows a MemberRole caller to PATCH a task they do not own, violating FR-009. The injection forces an Operation where a non-owner member patches a task owned by someone else.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_008_010_OwnerOrAdminEditDelete
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_010_OwnerOrAdminEditDelete: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Removing F_CrossTeamIsolation allows an Operation to target a task whose team differs from the operation's team context, directly violating the cross-team isolation invariant (FR-014 / SC-004). The injection forces such a cross-team access.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_MutationOperationsHaveAuditEntry  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_MutationOperationsHaveAuditEntry.als
    rationale: Removing F_MutationOperationsHaveAuditEntry allows a PatchTask operation to complete with no associated MutationEvent (no audit entry), violating FR-015 and SC-007. The injection forces a PatchTask operation with no MutationEvent.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerSave
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerSave: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerImmutability  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnerImmutability.als
    rationale: Removing F_OwnerImmutability allows an AuditCreated entry to record an actor different from the task's owner field, breaking the invariant that owner is set at creation and immutable. The injection forces a task whose owner does not match the creator recorded in the AuditCreated entry.
    expected to FAIL: FR_006_OwnerImmutability
      - FR_006_OwnerImmutability: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing F_PermissionMatrix frees the Allowed relation to contain any (Role, OperationKind) pairs, including granting MemberRole unconditional PatchTask/DeleteTask access, which would falsify LeastPrivilege. The injection adds that forbidden cell.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PrivilegeMonotonicity
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - PrivilegeMonotonicity: FAIL (expected)

